00:01:54.298 --> 00:01:56.924
- I would actually be,

00:01:56.924 --> 00:02:00.214
like I would be fired up happy.

00:02:00.214 --> 00:02:05.309
Because that is my game, not Elon's.

00:02:05.309 --> 00:02:06.969
And so I,

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:08.989
and this is the straight up truth.

00:02:08.989 --> 00:02:12.105
It is insane how I when
I hear that question,

00:02:12.105 --> 00:02:14.525
how obvious this is to me that I would

00:02:14.525 --> 00:02:17.476
absolutely destroy him and
he would fail miserably

00:02:17.476 --> 00:02:19.080
if he was trying to beat me in that game.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.721
In the same way that I would fail

00:02:20.721 --> 00:02:24.254
if I decided to, you
know, invent rocket ships

00:02:24.254 --> 00:02:27.682
into space and tesla cars
and things of that nature.

00:02:27.682 --> 00:02:30.711
When I play my game, whatever that is,

00:02:30.711 --> 00:02:33.210
building an agency,
building a wine retailer,

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.412
whatever I do next.

00:02:34.412 --> 00:02:35.888
If I'm operating, right?

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.575
Forget about investing where it's

00:02:37.575 --> 00:02:38.550
a little bit of a crapshoot.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.577
Forget about JVs where I have partners.

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:42.018
Me, me, Gary.

00:02:42.018 --> 00:02:44.697
If I'm operating, there's
not a single person

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.589
in the world that I'm
scared of at all ever

00:02:47.589 --> 00:02:49.630
because the only thing that can happen

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.623
is both of us getting ours.

00:02:52.623 --> 00:02:54.437
There is nobody that is going to beat me.

00:02:54.437 --> 00:02:55.906
The markets are too big.

00:02:55.906 --> 00:02:58.024
I'm going to get mines.

00:02:58.024 --> 00:03:01.218
And so, I'm not scare of Elon, or Shmelon,

00:03:01.218 --> 00:03:04.795
or Zucks, or Cubes, or Ashton,

00:03:04.795 --> 00:03:07.874
or anybody about anything

00:03:07.874 --> 00:03:09.929
that comes to do with
the game that I'm playing

00:03:09.929 --> 00:03:11.040
because I'm going to win.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.222
I'm going to win.

00:03:12.222 --> 00:03:14.040
Could they possibly do
more business than me?

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.179
Sure, I mean I'm not excited about that,

00:03:16.179 --> 00:03:17.378
but sure I guess it could happen.

00:03:17.378 --> 00:03:19.764
I don't think there's another
agency over the last 4 years

00:03:19.764 --> 00:03:22.929
that has grown at the size that we have,

00:03:22.929 --> 00:03:25.516
and in the liquor business
the same thing happened.

00:03:25.516 --> 00:03:26.792
But of course, somebody could

00:03:26.792 --> 00:03:28.141
come along with that kind of talent.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:31.178
But that's not going to
stop me from getting mine,

00:03:31.178 --> 00:03:35.457
and so the answer to your
question is I would be pumped

00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:36.693
because I think there
would be a lot of people

00:03:36.693 --> 00:03:38.871
talking about why didn't Elon use his mind

00:03:38.871 --> 00:03:41.421
and go and do start small businesses.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.598
And two, I would enjoy the
victory that I would get

00:03:43.598 --> 00:03:45.039
that would get me more screen cred

00:03:45.039 --> 00:03:46.391
for punching Elon in the mouth.

00:03:48.051 --> 00:03:50.230
- [Voiceover] James asks "Why
not go halves on the Jets

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.544
"or quarters and elevate the team

00:03:51.544 --> 00:03:53.064
"to the level only Gary could.

00:03:53.064 --> 00:03:55.074
"The owner has to see some
value in your methods.

00:03:55.074 --> 00:03:56.722
"Seems like this might be something

00:03:56.722 --> 00:03:58.531
"more realistic and attained sooner.

00:03:58.531 --> 00:03:59.929
"Is it all or nothing?"

00:03:59.929 --> 00:04:01.735
- James, it's all or nothing mainly

00:04:01.735 --> 00:04:03.178
because the owner's not interested.

00:04:03.178 --> 00:04:05.143
I mean, Woody Johnson is a billionaire.

00:04:05.143 --> 00:04:06.990
He's doing his thing.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.246
He's not outwardly reaching out to me.

00:04:10.246 --> 00:04:13.491
He's rolling in going about his merry way.

00:04:13.491 --> 00:04:16.043
And that's that.

00:04:16.043 --> 00:04:18.096
And he's in control of that situation.

00:04:18.096 --> 00:04:19.204
I'm not worried about it.

00:04:19.204 --> 00:04:21.380
I'm focusing on what I can control,

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.081
which is amass enough wealth and power

00:04:25.081 --> 00:04:29.816
and opportunity and narrative
and leverage and branding

00:04:29.816 --> 00:04:32.532
to give me the best shot
to actually pull this off.

00:04:32.532 --> 00:04:35.002
And so that's why.

00:04:35.002 --> 00:04:37.298
Plus I would never go in for an ask.

00:04:37.298 --> 00:04:38.530
Right, I would never be like

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.458
"Hello Mr. Johnson, why don't you

00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:42.800
"sell me 25% of the company"
or things of that nature.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.125
Just not in me.

00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:46.700
I'm going to take it if I deserve it.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.714
I'll get it if I'm good enough.

00:04:48.714 --> 00:04:51.384
And so I'm focusing
every piece of my energy

00:04:51.384 --> 00:04:54.713
doing things to put me in that position

00:04:54.713 --> 00:04:56.524
because the amount of luck and serendipity

00:04:56.524 --> 00:04:58.786
that has to happen for me
to even get that at bat,

00:04:58.786 --> 00:05:01.612
literally the passing of the company on,

00:05:01.612 --> 00:05:03.180
whatever Woody decides to do with it,

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.141
hopefully, hopefully he
owns it his whole life

00:05:05.141 --> 00:05:06.850
and hopefully he lives
for a very long time

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.620
and hopefully because I'm much younger

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.081
I'm there in a position
to make that purchase

00:05:11.081 --> 00:05:13.665
if his family doesn't
want to hold onto it.

00:05:13.665 --> 00:05:15.596
So there's just a million
different variables

00:05:15.596 --> 00:05:19.261
that come into play that
have to fall into place

00:05:19.261 --> 00:05:21.232
but I just need to focus
on what I can control

00:05:21.232 --> 00:05:23.081
and really for everybody,
that's the biggest thing.

00:05:23.081 --> 00:05:24.523
Way too many of you, and I've been really

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.948
digging into my community in
the last three or four days.

00:05:26.948 --> 00:05:28.759
A lot of, this has actually

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:30.043
turned into a really good question.

00:05:30.043 --> 00:05:33.489
A lot of you just worrying
about shit you can't control.

00:05:33.489 --> 00:05:35.500
Like, it's unbelievable.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.062
I don't know what's the matter with you.

00:05:37.062 --> 00:05:40.060
Like you can't control it, the end.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.454
Like it's not super complicated.

00:05:41.454 --> 00:05:43.006
You can't control the weather.

00:05:43.006 --> 00:05:43.942
You can't.

00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:45.710
Like, people literally
crying that it rained

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.309
during their like flea market or food fair

00:05:48.309 --> 00:05:49.417
or I don't remember exactly what it was.

00:05:49.417 --> 00:05:50.484
Like, okay.

00:05:50.484 --> 00:05:52.325
But like, like, and then
like, then I was like

00:05:52.325 --> 00:05:53.316
okay maybe it was just a single rant.

00:05:53.316 --> 00:05:54.841
But like seven tweets, I'm like wha.

00:05:54.841 --> 00:05:56.237
Like it rained.

00:05:56.237 --> 00:05:58.702
Like Mother Nature (censored) you.

00:05:58.702 --> 00:06:00.266
Take it like a woman.

00:06:00.266 --> 00:06:02.153
And like, you know, and so, you know.

00:06:02.153 --> 00:06:06.212
I just don't believe in crying

00:06:06.212 --> 00:06:07.922
over things you can not control.

00:06:07.922 --> 00:06:11.050
And so I just think about
the things I can control

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:14.090
and so please try to take this answer

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.650
and understand how important it is

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.382
to not dwell but instead reverse it

00:06:19.382 --> 00:06:22.017
and think about what you can
be doing during that time.

00:06:22.017 --> 00:06:23.866
You know if it rained, when it rained

00:06:23.866 --> 00:06:25.589
during times I've done flea markets,

00:06:25.589 --> 00:06:29.044
I packed up and went dollar
store and Toys R Us shopping.

00:06:29.044 --> 00:06:31.308
You know, I didn't just
sit there and take my rain.

00:06:34.338 --> 00:06:35.158
- [India] Was good.

00:06:35.158 --> 00:06:36.146
- Yeah.

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:38.289
- [Voiceover] Yannick
asks "What's your opinion

00:06:38.289 --> 00:06:39.850
"on always wanting more in life?

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.105
"Good, bad, and why?"

00:06:42.105 --> 00:06:44.440
- That's a really good question.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.201
My point of view on this is both.

00:06:47.201 --> 00:06:50.731
Always wanting more in life seriously

00:06:50.731 --> 00:06:54.267
while being very very content
and happy at the same time.

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:55.499
That's what I am.

00:06:55.499 --> 00:06:57.664
You know, this is
something you may not know.

00:06:57.664 --> 00:06:59.870
Though I would be disappointed,

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.848
and my ego, boy my ego
which is a nice part of me,

00:07:02.848 --> 00:07:06.835
would really take a hit,
if a little weird genie

00:07:06.835 --> 00:07:09.256
showed up right now, weird genie, got it?

00:07:09.256 --> 00:07:10.485
Boom!

00:07:10.485 --> 00:07:12.007
If the weird genie said to me,

00:07:12.007 --> 00:07:14.267
"Hey Gary, I'm the weird
genie of the future.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:17.430
"Bad news, you're not
going to grow anymore!

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.033
"This is it, you've plateaued!"

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:20.680
I'd be like, oh!

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.627
Like a big shot.

00:07:21.627 --> 00:07:22.689
But I'd be like, all right.

00:07:22.689 --> 00:07:26.146
Like, to me, like, I've
had a great run already.

00:07:26.146 --> 00:07:29.070
Like, I've done really well.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.319
And many people would be really happy

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:34.243
to have these professional
accolades and successes

00:07:34.243 --> 00:07:36.735
as their entire life's work.

00:07:36.735 --> 00:07:39.900
That would rip my heart
out of my body right now

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.961
if that were to be true.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.348
You don't have to animate
them ripping my heart out.

00:07:44.348 --> 00:07:47.063
No Mortal Kombat shit here.

00:07:47.063 --> 00:07:50.932
But it is probably
surprising to some of you

00:07:50.932 --> 00:07:52.453
because I don't talk about it as much

00:07:52.453 --> 00:07:54.382
how content I actually am.

00:07:54.382 --> 00:07:57.467
And so my point of view on
it is a very strong balance

00:07:57.467 --> 00:08:00.265
of happiness and content
with what you've got

00:08:00.265 --> 00:08:02.963
while being very hungry

00:08:02.963 --> 00:08:06.633
and striving for real real victories

00:08:06.633 --> 00:08:08.866
and upside and the climb and the game.

00:08:08.866 --> 00:08:10.299
And so that's where I'm at.

00:08:10.299 --> 00:08:11.492
And as you can imagine,

00:08:11.492 --> 00:08:12.941
as you're probably listening to this,

00:08:12.941 --> 00:08:14.751
that makes me very happy.

00:08:14.751 --> 00:08:18.028
Like, it's probably a big
reason I'm so damn happy.

00:08:18.028 --> 00:08:19.929
It's a nice place to be.

00:08:21.639 --> 00:08:22.959
You like that?

00:08:22.959 --> 00:08:23.701
- [India] Yeah.

00:08:23.701 --> 00:08:24.563
- Thanks India.

00:08:24.563 --> 00:08:26.271
I'm ripping it with you today.
- [India] Yeah.

00:08:26.271 --> 00:08:27.367
- Yeah.

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:28.760
Really winning India over.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:30.947
- Every episode.

00:08:30.947 --> 00:08:31.929
- Thank you.

00:08:31.929 --> 00:08:32.873
- It's Robin Norgren with

00:08:32.873 --> 00:08:35.580
faithandcreativity.com
and Joseys Art School

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.605
thanking you for all that you
share with us entrepreneurs

00:08:39.605 --> 00:08:41.262
or would-be entrepreneurs.

00:08:41.262 --> 00:08:44.260
So my question is that
Hulu made a decision

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:47.041
recently to offer subscribers the option

00:08:47.041 --> 00:08:51.551
to have ad-free subscriptions

00:08:51.551 --> 00:08:53.941
and wanted to know what
your thoughts are on that.

00:08:53.941 --> 00:08:57.436
We will keep asking questions.

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:59.805
I'm so glad that you keep answering them.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:00.836
Thanks Gary Vee.

00:09:00.836 --> 00:09:03.213
- You got it, thank you
for such a darling video.

00:09:03.213 --> 00:09:04.601
Loved your earrings by the way.

00:09:04.601 --> 00:09:06.462
I think it's a smart business model.

00:09:06.462 --> 00:09:07.817
Some people value time,

00:09:07.817 --> 00:09:10.369
hate ads enough to pay for a subscription.

00:09:10.369 --> 00:09:13.076
Other people are willing
to go the other route.

00:09:13.076 --> 00:09:14.519
They don't want to pay
for the subscription.

00:09:14.519 --> 00:09:17.229
I think giving customers
two or three options.

00:09:17.229 --> 00:09:19.116
My preference is three.

00:09:19.116 --> 00:09:20.264
I think there's a lot of interesting

00:09:20.264 --> 00:09:24.512
psycho-data around that,
to how they want to

00:09:24.512 --> 00:09:27.840
experience a platform is very very smart.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.201
I think it lends itself
to higher profit margins,

00:09:31.201 --> 00:09:32.928
especially when you do three.

00:09:32.928 --> 00:09:36.093
And so I think that's a
very smart move by Hulu.

00:09:36.093 --> 00:09:40.509
I do not believe that one,
especially if you're a platform,

00:09:40.509 --> 00:09:43.068
one option is the way to go.

00:09:43.068 --> 00:09:46.751
As a matter of fact, if I
ever do a book by myself,

00:09:46.751 --> 00:09:49.428
self-publish, because I'm a free agent

00:09:49.428 --> 00:09:50.945
after this next book comes out.

00:09:50.945 --> 00:09:52.097
That's right Harper Collins.

00:09:52.097 --> 00:09:53.461
Call me back.

00:09:53.461 --> 00:09:55.352
(laughter)

00:09:58.012 --> 00:10:00.435
I would probably do
some really interesting

00:10:00.435 --> 00:10:01.745
three different pricing models

00:10:01.745 --> 00:10:02.980
where you get different options.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.657
I think there's interesting
dynamics around that.

00:10:04.657 --> 00:10:06.873
So I think Hulu made
a very smart decision.

